# Local bookkeeping — describes the state of Daniel's machine, not the site.
# .build-stamps.json records what a build was made FROM. Not served, and it would churn the history
# on every publish. (.canvas-pasted.json sat here too, recording which ?v= had been pasted into
# Canvas; the Canvas Pages were retired 2026-09-07 and the file went with them.)
.build-stamps.json
.DS_Store

# Never, under any circumstances. The salt derives every published folder name (site_build.site_salt)
# and lives in class-manager/, outside this tree — this line is the belt to that braces. The
# credential likewise lives one level up, outside the repo, so it cannot be added even by `git add -A`.
.site-salt
github-credential.txt
